    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-08-06T21:20:37+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-06T21:20:37+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-06T11:50:37Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-06T11:50:37Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A weak high pressure system centred over NSW will slowly move east while maintaining a ridge over SA until Saturday. A strong cold front will then begin to move into the Bight and move east over the state from late Saturday and throughout Sunday. Another cold front is then forecast to move into the Bight from late Monday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW010" description="West Coast" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-08-06T21:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-07T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-06T11:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-06T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly clear. Slight chance of a shower west of Nullarbor, near zero chance elsewhere. Winds east to northeasterly 15 to 20 km/h.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-08-07T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-08T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-06T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-07T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Very high chance of showers. The chance of a thunderstorm west of Nullarbor. Winds north to northeasterly 20 to 30 km/h tending north to northwesterly 15 to 25 km/h in the late evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 5 and 11 with daytime temperatures reaching between 19 and 25.</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 10:50am to 2:30pm, UV Index predicted to reach 4 [Moderate]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-08-08T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-09T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-07T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-08T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Very high chance of showers, most likely in the late afternoon and evening. The chance of a thunderstorm near the coast in the evening. Winds north to northwesterly 20 to 30 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to around 8 with daytime temperatures reaching the low 20s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-08-09T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-10T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-08T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-09T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. Very high chance of showers, most likely in the morning and afternoon with possible small hail west of Nullarbor. The chance of a thunderstorm south of Streaky Bay in the morning. Winds west to northwesterly 20 to 30 km/h tending west to southwesterly 35 to 50 km/h during the day. Overnight temperatures falling to between 4 and 7 with daytime temperatures reaching around 14.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="4" start-time-local="2026-08-10T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-11T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-09T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-10T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. High chance of showers south of Streaky Bay, medium chance elsewhere. Winds westerly 20 to 30 km/h turning northwesterly 25 to 35 km/h during the day. Overnight temperatures falling to between 4 and 7 with daytime temperatures reaching around 17.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
